{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"f88b0bd68640c04f","name":"card_unit_usaaf_spitfire_ix","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/Breakthrough/units/card_unit_usaaf_spitfire_ix","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"USAAF SPITFIRE IX","text":"Deployment: Draw a random air unit from your deck.","flavorText":"The Supermarine Spitfire was a British fighter aircraft that was used during WWII, mainly by RAF, but also by their allies. Around 600 Spitfires served in the US Army Air Force and the Navy and it was one of the few foreign aircraft to do so. The Spitfire Mk IX variant first entered service in 1941 and became very successful in countering the newly developed German fighter, namely the Focke-Wulf Fw 190, and such was the Mk IX’s success that it became the second most produced Spitfire during the war. The Mk IX usually had an armament of 2 × 20 mm Hispano II cannon, 2 × 0.50 or 4 x 0.303 Browning M2 machine guns and capacity of carrying 2 x 110 kg bombs in the wing racket and 1 x 230 kg bomb in the center racket.","faction":"USA","type":"fighter","rarity":"Rare","cost":7,"operationCost":2,"attack":5,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["subtype.spitfire"],"Name":"card_unit_usaaf_spitfire_ix","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_usaaf_spitfire_ix_title","SourceString":"USAAF SPITFIRE IX","LocalizedString":"USAAF SPITFIRE IX"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":5,"defense":5,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":7,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_usaaf_spitfire_ix_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Draw a random air unit from your deck.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Draw a random air unit from your deck."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_usaaf_spitfire_ix_history","SourceString":"The Supermarine Spitfire was a British fighter aircraft that was used during WWII, mainly by RAF, but also by their allies. Around 600 Spitfires served in the US Army Air Force and the Navy and it was one of the few foreign aircraft to do so. The Spitfire Mk IX variant first entered service in 1941 and became very successful in countering the newly developed German fighter, namely the Focke-Wulf Fw 190, and such was the Mk IX’s success that it became the second most produced Spitfire during the war. The Mk IX usually had an armament of 2 × 20 mm Hispano II cannon, 2 × 0.50 or 4 x 0.303 Browning M2 machine guns and capacity of carrying 2 x 110 kg bombs in the wing racket and 1 x 230 kg bomb in the center racket.","LocalizedString":"The Supermarine Spitfire was a British fighter aircraft that was used during WWII, mainly by RAF, but also by their allies. Around 600 Spitfires served in the US Army Air Force and the Navy and it was one of the few foreign aircraft to do so. The Spitfire Mk IX variant first entered service in 1941 and became very successful in countering the newly developed German fighter, namely the Focke-Wulf Fw 190, and such was the Mk IX’s success that it became the second most produced Spitfire during the war. The Mk IX usually had an armament of 2 × 20 mm Hispano II cannon, 2 × 0.50 or 4 x 0.303 Browning M2 machine guns and capacity of carrying 2 x 110 kg bombs in the wing racket and 1 x 230 kg bomb in the center racket."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","isReserved":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Deployment"],"hasDeployment":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_Exp_Aircraft_Large_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Card_Blowups/AU_Exp_Aircraft_Large_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/DontUseOrTemp/usa_spitfire.usa_spitfire","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Roy Grinnell","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/USAAF_SPITFIRE_IX.USAAF_SPITFIRE_IX","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":328.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_